"""What people say about their own lives, as meaning (roles) and sentence frames.

Every fact kind has:
  layer   how far they must trust you before they'll say it (see inner.py)
  roles   the facts of it, chosen once for the person and kept: which knee, what broke it, which remedy
  beats   what happened / the proof of it / what they do about it. Each beat is a list of sentence
          shapes; sentences.py fills them from the roles and the shared word lists in LEX.

A shape should be *built*, not written out whole: a few slots, each filled from a list, so one fact
comes out dozens or hundreds of ways while saying the same thing. "{part.subj.cap} {ache.v} whenever
{foul} {coming}" is one shape and well over a hundred sentences.

Roles and LEX entries are strings, or {"text": ..., "num": "pl"} for a plural (so verbs agree), and
may contain slots of their own. Slot syntax is in sentences.py.
"""


def P(text):
    """A plural noun phrase: verbs after it agree ('my knees ache')."""
    return {"text": text, "num": "pl"}


